+# LOSSY-VERIFICATION PILOT PATCH (not upstream vLLM). "Judge + nudge":
+# spec-casc-tok-free-judgment's own "extended verification span" trick
+# (EAGLE verification is already ONE parallel forward pass over the whole
+# drafted block, so appending fixed tokens after the real draft lets the
+# target's SAME pass compute more real logits at marginal FLOPs cost),
+# combined with two separately-validated findings from this investigation
+# instead of free-judgment's own reject-and-resample actuator (proven, via
+# a real 6-case rollout AND a positionally-verified causal trace on
+# case_010, to do more harm than good -- resampling from an UNMODIFIED
+# target distribution barely moves a stuck reasoning state):
+#   1. The best-performing free-judgment criterion phrase of six tested
+#      against 48 real ground-truth-labeled points (ANALYSIS/semantic_
+#      guard/README.md): a TRUE/FALSE declarative judgment with an
+#      explicit completion-forcing scaffold, specifically strongest on
+#      confirmed semantic reasoning loops (not just literal repetition).
+#   2. spec-casc-tok-rv's own ephemeral logit-blend actuator (see that
+#      patch's own module comment) -- ephemeral, never committed to
+#      persistent context, closing the exact gap reject-and-resample had.
+#
+# ORIGINALLY designed as a 3-stage screen->verify->nudge pipeline, gating
+# the wide (judge/nudge) rounds behind a cheap always-on hidden-state-
+# recurrence screen so the width tax would only be paid when something
+# looked suspicious. That screen stage was DROPPED after a real,
+# empirical test: making free-judgment's own criterion-append conditional
+# (fire 1/20 rounds, num_speculative_tokens left at the same fixed 29)
+# measured 0.02807 s/round -- statistically identical to the ALWAYS-wide
+# baseline (0.02799 s/round), not the genuinely-narrow one (0.01250
+# s/round). num_speculative_tokens is a static, server-startup-fixed
+# config; the SCHEDULER (not this patch) decides how many tokens get
+# verified each round, and always schedules the full configured width
+# regardless of what content this patch puts there. There is no live
+# per-round lever to make some rounds cheap and others expensive within
+# this repo's patch scope. See analysis/semantic_guard/
+# DESIGN_screen_verify_nudge.md for the full design history including
+# this amendment.
+#
+# Net effect: this mechanism pays the wide-verification tax EVERY round,
+# unconditionally, same order of cost as free-judgment's own criterion
+# (measured ~+150%/round for a comparable width) -- an accepted cost, not
+# an oversight.
+#
+# Round layout (row 0 -- single-real-sequence-per-process scoping, same
+# convention as this repo's other cross-round-state patches):
+#   JUDGE mode (default): [0:REAL_DRAFT_LEN) real draft, then the fixed
+#     TRUE/FALSE judge criterion pattern.
+#   NUDGE mode (only while rejection_sampler.py's own nudge_remaining
+#     counter is > 0): [0:REAL_DRAFT_LEN) real draft, then the fixed
+#     reflection prompt, then a literal COPY of the real draft tokens
+#     (spec-casc-tok-rv's own layout, reused verbatim).
+# NUM_SPEC is configured as max(REAL_DRAFT_LEN + JUDGE_LEN,
+# 2*REAL_DRAFT_LEN + RV_PROMPT_LEN) so both patterns always fit; whichever
+# pattern is shorter just leaves its own trailing columns as whatever
+# EAGLE itself drafted there -- harmless, since both patterns always
+# force-reject at their own first token, so nothing past that boundary is
+# ever reached by the round's own accept/reject walk regardless of what's
+# in the unused tail.
+_JN_REAL_DRAFT_LEN_FILE = f"/tmp/lossy-token-eff-judge-nudge-real-draft-len-{os.getuid()}"
+try:
+    with open(_JN_REAL_DRAFT_LEN_FILE) as _f:
+        _JN_REAL_DRAFT_LEN = int(float(_f.read().strip()))
+except (OSError, ValueError):
+    _JN_REAL_DRAFT_LEN = 0  # 0 = disabled (no-op), the safe default
+
+# Judge criterion, tokenized once via openai_harmony's HARMONY_GPT_OSS
+# encoding, pinned as a literal constant (same convention as every other
+# fixed-phrase patch in this repo). The best of six phrasings tested
+# against 48 real ground-truth-labeled points (see
+# analysis/semantic_guard/README.md): a declarative TRUE/FALSE judgment
+# with an explicit completion-forcing scaffold ("the answer is:" -- same
+# lesson as free-judgment's own six-phrase iteration: without an explicit
+# completion constraint, the model just keeps explaining instead of
+# answering). Text (the "FLASE" typo is deliberate -- literally what was
+# tested and validated; untested whether correcting it changes anything):
+#   "\n\nThe last few tokens are unproductively repetitive. Answer TRUE
+#    or FLASE: the answer is:"
+_JN_JUDGE_PATTERN = [
+    279, 976, 2174, 3120, 20290, 553, 537, 5260, 5861, 93185, 13, 30985,
+    19894, 503, 17134, 8925, 25, 290, 6052, 382, 25,
+]
+_JN_JUDGE_LEN = len(_JN_JUDGE_PATTERN)
+
